 "summary": "Family of assembly languages for the Intel x86 instruction set architecture and its 64-bit AMD64/Intel 64 extension, written in Intel syntax (MASM, NASM, YASM, FASM) or AT&T syntax (GNU as); each assembler adds its own directives, macro system and expression language on top of the vendor-defined instruction set.",
 "status": "active",
