 "influenced_by": [],
 "related": [{"id": "c", "relation": "family"}, {"id": "llvm-ir", "relation": "compiles-to"}],
 "level_notes": {"1": "The instruction set is defined by vendor manuals (Intel SDM, AMD APM; no independent standard). Each assembler's manual defines its syntax and directives (NASM manual, GNU as manual, Microsoft MASM reference). Calling conventions are defined by the System V psABI documents (x86-64 and i386) and Microsoft's x64 conventions. x86-TSO is the accepted formal memory model.", "2": "Felix Cloutier's HTML extraction of the SDM instruction reference is listed at level 2 as a derived guide; tutorials and university guides cover both syntaxes.", "3": "Wikipedia, PLDB and Rosetta Code (Rosetta reports blocked from the sandbox)."},
